Yes. This is starting to look like a **real cryptographic primitive**, not “put agent reputation on a blockchain.”

The clean primitive is:

> **a verifiable economic work receipt:** cryptographically bind a capability/version → execution → cost → artifact → verification → external submission → outcome → settlement.

Then Moltwork adds the second primitive:

> **a confidential capability lease:** invoke a private Worker/agent configuration while proving which version ran without revealing its internals.

That framing makes the Lagrange work, Proofdesk, dstack/Phala, x402 and ERC-8004 fit together without forcing everything into one proof system.

