### I found an audit bug worth fixing

The current `LedgerEvent` stores:

```text
payload
payload_hash
```

but `verify_chain()` recomputes the event hash using the **stored `payload_hash`** without first recomputing:

```text
SHA256(payload) == payload_hash
```

So the unsealed-chain verifier doesn't independently detect payload mutation if someone changes the payload while preserving the old `payload_hash`. Also, `timestamp` isn't included in the event hash body.

Easy fix:

```text
verify event:
    recompute payload_hash
    verify payload_hash

    recompute event_hash
    verify event_hash

    verify prev_event_hash

    verify timestamp/seq included
```

And an epoch root isn't actually trustworthy merely because it exists locally — you need to **sign or externally anchor the root**.

So Proofdesk gave you 80% of the local ledger. Sigstore/chain anchoring supplies the missing trust boundary.

