# Proof tiers become composable

Don't call an entire run simply `verified=true`.

| Claim                                        | Possible proof                      |
| -------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| Artifact hasn't changed                      | SHA-256                             |
| Event was in run                             | Merkle inclusion                    |
| Worker owner signed it                       | DSSE/Sigstore                       |
| Exact WorkerKit runtime ran it               | dstack/Phala TEE                    |
| Exact secret Worker configuration was loaded | TEE + attestation-gated key release |
| Model actually produced output               | DeepProve                           |
| Output passed evaluator                      | SVR/verifier attestation            |
| Platform says accepted                       | authenticated API / signed receipt  |
| Payment happened                             | onchain transaction                 |
| Historical reputation calculation is correct | eventually Lagrange Coprocessor     |

That's far more credible than inventing one giant ZK proof.

