# Does Moltwork become a crypto primitive?

**Yes, if you keep the blockchain portion narrow.**

WorkerKit itself remains:

> framework-neutral economic execution runtime.

Moltwork becomes:

> **the protocol for exchanging, leasing, verifying and settling machine capabilities and their work receipts.**

The actual crypto primitives are:

```text
WorkerAsset
WorkerLease
WorkerRunReceipt
OutcomeReceipt
SettlementReceipt
AttestationRegistry
```

x402 gives you payment.

dstack gives you confidential execution.

DeepProve can give you inference correctness.

Sigstore/in-toto gives provenance.

The chain gives:

```text
identity
timestamp/ordering
public commitments
leases
payments
settlement
portable reputation
```

That is a coherent crypto product.

It is **not**:

> put a marketplace database on Ethereum.

